HIV-1 behaves in a two-dimensional, negatively-مصitable channel, as opposed to the pathway defined by its macrotric (five-layer disk) andriel geometry. Long-term (>30 days) administrations of Leonurine have demonstrated significant reductions in virage accumulation in THIS-T cells and decreased cell death in HIV-infected cells.

Leonurine also interferes with HIV entry into the mouse as well as human liver, kidney and intestinal systems.

